<SiteLayout title="Sources and research coverage · Historica" description="See what has been checked, what is provisional and where Historica still has gaps. Explore the linked sources and research coverage." path="/coverage.html" page="coverage">

<header><a class="brand" href="./">historica</a><span class="beta-sash">BETA</span><span class="brand-tagline">Visualising history</span><a class="return" href="./">Home</a><a href="/about">About</a><ThemeControl /></header>
<div class="beta-notice">Research coverage · Missing records mean gaps in our research, not an absence of history.</div>
<main><p class="eyebrow">THE WORLD · 3000 BCE TO 200 CE</p><h1>How much of history can we see?</h1><p class="intro">Historica is a growing collection, not a complete account of the world. Every entry should make its sources and limitations easy to find.</p>
<section class="research-guide" aria-label="Understanding the research"><article><h2>Checked against sources</h2><p>Some individual statements have been compared with the linked source passages. Their evidence is available on the entry.</p><p id="checked-total"></p><p>These checks use AI assistance. They are not independent expert review.</p></article><article><h2>Still provisional</h2><p>Some entries currently have reading references, but their individual statements have not all been checked. Dates or descriptions may change as we review them.</p><p>Open “Dates, sources and caveats” on a timeline page to see its status.</p></article><article><h2>Still incomplete</h2><p>A sourced entry does not mean we have covered its whole region or period. Everyday life and less documented places need much more work.</p><p>An empty part of the timeline means missing research, not that nothing happened there.</p></article></section>
<details class="research-plan"><summary>Explore the detailed research plan</summary><p>This planning grid tracks broad regional overviews. A region only counts as complete when all its themes have been covered, so these totals do not measure how many individual timeline statements have been checked.</p><p id="error" role="alert" hidden></p>
<section id="totals" class="totals" aria-label="Worldwide coverage totals"></section><p id="revision" class="muted"></p>
<div class="coverage-layout"><section><h2>Places through time</h2><div class="coverage-filters"><label>Region group <select id="group"><option value="all">Everywhere</option></select></label><label>Workflow <select id="workflow"><option value="all">All stages</option></select></label><label>Evidence <select id="evidence-filter"><option value="all">All evidence outcomes</option></select></label><label class="pilot"><input id="pilot" type="checkbox"> Pilot packages only</label></div>
<p class="legend">U · Unresearched &nbsp; G · Gathering &nbsp; D · Drafted &nbsp; C · Checking &nbsp; A · Accepted<br>Evidence: ? Unknown &nbsp; S Substantive &nbsp; L Limited</p><p id="match-count" role="status"></p><div class="matrix-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Research coverage table; scroll horizontally for later periods"><table id="matrix"></table></div><p class="muted">Each cell is a research package. Select one to see its scope and outstanding work. These areas and time windows organise research; they are not historical borders or periods.</p></section>
<aside id="package-detail" aria-label="Selected research package"></aside></div>
<section id="research-findings" class="research-findings" aria-label="Draft research findings"></section><section id="supplementary" class="supplementary"></section></details><footer><p><a href="/coverage.html">Sources and research coverage</a> · <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></p>Check the linked sources when a detail matters. We show uncertainty where we know about it, and revise entries as the research improves.<p>Historica is an open source site on <a href="https://github.com/sproates/historica">GitHub</a>.</p></footer></main>
</SiteLayout>
